# perf-lean -- DROPS ONLY.  The peripheral payload a perf leg never touches.
#
# Copyright 2026 by Frobenius Norm LLC 2026-11-12
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS, MEASURED 2026-11-12 ON esp32s3-n32r16-00.  A `--class citable` perf leg boots the
# board TWICE PER INDEX -- 252 boots for a 126-index BC,NCG run -- and each boot is ~9.3 s, of which
# ~3 s is loading drivers for hardware no benchmark touches:
#
#     LCD1602.scm   1,825 ms   <- the single largest item in the whole boot
#     I2C.scm         238 ms
#     PCA9685         115 ms + 110 ms probing a device that is not attached ("No device at 95")
#     bacnet.scm      293 ms   (BACnet/IP ready, A-side + B-side)
#     csv, array, llip-auth, base64, rsa, dh_groups   the rest
#
# At 252 boots that is ~13 minutes per leg spent initialising an LCD, an I2C bus, a servo driver and
# a building-automation stack in order to time `fib-rec`.  The owner called the 2.5 h leg a
# productivity impairment; this is the part of it that costs nothing scientifically to remove.
#
# EVERY DROP BELOW IS `file-exists?`-GUARDED IN setup.scm, WHICH IS WHY THIS IS SAFE.  Checked line
# by line before writing it: Sonar 433, I2C 435, Wire 436, PCA9685 437, PCF8574 438, LCD1602 449,
# base64 452, rsa 453, dh_groups 454, llip-auth 455, csv 456, bacnet 457, llip-serial 447,
# llip-server 814.  An omitted file is simply absent and setup.scm steps over it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* DROPPED, because setup.scm loads it UNCONDITIONALLY and an absent file
# would fail the boot rather than be skipped:
#     Compiler.scm Terminal.scm Lobs.scm Behaviors.scm Pins.scm Timers.scm ESP32.scm CommonIO.scm
#     Buzzer.scm (423)  WiFi.scm (434)  WS2812.scm (439)  LightSensor.scm (448)  rxrs/*
# Buzzer stays for a second reason: the startup beep is ONE 5 ms tone at 400 Hz, specified by the
# owner 2026-09-25 as the board's readiness signal, and it is 5 ms -- not a cost worth touching.
#
# AND THE BENCH FILES THE LEG DOES NOT RUN GO TOO.  gc-pause-bench, pause_bench and
# ncg-fusion-probe are separate tests with their own legs; they are staged here only because the
# board manifest ships one image for every test.
#
# A DROP IS MATCHED ON THE *DESTINATION*, not the source path -- see _w3_manifest_expand.  So a
# `file: tests/ll_tests/x.scm -> ll_tests/x.scm` entry is dropped by its right-hand side.

# A DROP IS MATCHED ON THE LINE'S DESTINATION, AND FOR A BARE ENTRY THAT IS THE PATH AS WRITTEN --
# `core/LCD1602.scm`, NOT `LCD1602.scm`.  The matcher is `d="${line##*->}"`, which for an entry with
# no `->` returns the whole line.  Written with basenames first, this file dropped NOTHING and the
# lean image came out byte-identical to the full one, with the drop list sitting here looking
# applied.  `Freenove-ESP32-WROVER-sd.manifest` is the worked example and uses full source paths.

-core/Sonar.scm
-core/I2C.scm
-core/Wire.scm
-core/PCA9685.scm
-core/PCF8574.scm
-core/LCD1602.scm
-features/base64.scm
-features/rsa.scm
-features/dh_groups.scm
-features/llip-auth.scm
-features/csv.scm
-features/bacnet.scm
-features/llip-serial.scm
-tools/llip-server.scm
-ll_tests/gc-pause-bench.scm
-ll_tests/pause_bench.scm
-ll_tests/ncg-fusion-probe.scm
